WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.450
Undoubtedly one of modern history’s most
notorious and abhorrent killers -- his crimes

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.720
are the stuff of nightmares.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.660
Over the course of 13 years, he prowled for
men and lured them back to his house before

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.980
drugging and strangling them.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.929
In all he took the lives of 17 men between
1978 and 1991.

00:00:19.929 --> 00:00:23.660
But simply killing his victims wasn’t enough
for Jeffrey Dahmer.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.929
He never wanted them to leave him so he saved
“trophies” — including severed heads.

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:32.160
Eventually, he ate parts of his victims.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:37.329
Dahmer was captured in 1991 and sentenced
to 16 life terms.

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:41.250
He was killed by fellow prison inmate Christopher
Scarver in 1994.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:45.430
Today let’s take a look back on the serial
killer’s life.

00:00:45.430 --> 00:01:02.420
Early Life

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.430
Jeffrey Dahmer was born on May 21, 1960 in
Milwaukee, Wisconsin to Lionel and Joyce Dahmer.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:12.950
He was described by his mother as a beautiful
baby, and both parents considered him to be

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.640
a normal child.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.000
His teachers saw him differently.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.049
At least one — his first grade teacher -- wondered
if Jeffrey was neglected at home and noted

00:01:22.049 --> 00:01:24.400
he was a reserved child on his report card.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.610
It’s true, both of Jeffrey’s parents didn’t
spend a lot of time with him.

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:32.440
When Jeffrey was young, his father was in
college earning his chemistry degree and Jeffrey’s

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.430
mother was often bedridden recovering from
illnesses.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:40.899
Jeffrey’s parents had a tumultuous marriage
that he later described as “extreme tension”

00:01:40.899 --> 00:01:42.659
from the constant arguing at home.

00:01:42.659 --> 00:01:47.860
Yet, there was no doubt Lionel and Joyce Dahmer
loved their son and tried to do the best for

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:48.860
him.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.890
When he was six years old, worried Jeffrey
might not take well to a new baby brother,

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.750
they let him pick out his name.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.119
Jeffrey named his younger brother David.

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:02.409
The Dahmer family moved a few times before
eventually settling in Bath, Ohio in 1968.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:06.530
If there were any red flags that indicated
future violence in the young Jeffrey, it was

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.520
his fascination with animal bones and how
they “fit together.”

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.660
The interest in carcasses began when he was
four years old.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.440
One day, Jeffrey was helping his father clear
animal remains from under the house and Jeffrey

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.810
was “oddly thrilled” by the sound of the
bones dropping into the metal bucket.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:26.160
He later started collecting them; searching
in ditches and along streets for roadkill.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.360
He began dismembering the bodies behind the
house in a patch of wooded area and stored

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.830
the various body parts in jars in the family’s
woodshed.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:39.640
On one occasion, Jeffrey decapitated the corpse
of a dog before nailing the body to a tree.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:43.300
When he was ten years old, over dinner, Jeffrey
asked his father what would happen if chicken

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.130
bones were placed in bleach.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:50.320
Lionel, a chemist, interpreted his son’s
question as mere scientific curiosity and

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:56.060
he took the opportunity to teach his son about
the proper way to clean and preserve his collections.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:02.170
Jeffrey later admitted at the age of 14 he
began experiencing sexual “compulsions.”

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:07.510
He desired boys, not girls, and the sexual
fantasies involved submission, violence, and

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.510
death.

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:12.910
He began drinking as a teenager to suppress
his urges and didn’t talk to anyone about

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:14.930
the disturbing thoughts he was having.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:20.260
At the age of 16, he fantasized about raping
a jogger he saw regularly and planned to attack

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.260
the man.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.030
One day Jeffrey lay in wait with a baseball
bat in the bushes along the man’s regular

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.030
route.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.970
The man didn’t come by that day, and Jeffrey
never attempted to carry it out again.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:34.790
At Revere High School, most of his classmates
thought of Dahmer as an outcast with a few

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:37.400
friends; some were troubled by his heavy drinking.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.170
He drank both beer and liquor while at school
by smuggling it inside the lining of his army

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.170
fatigue jacket.

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:47.880
His grades were average and then took a dive
as his drinking spun out of control in 1977.

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:51.120
He played clarinet briefly in band, and was
a decent tennis player.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.130
Overall, his teachers observed Jeffrey as
polite and quiet.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:59.470
Although he was awkward, he regularly amused
his classmates by staging pranks such as acting

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:03.580
out seizures, knocking over items, and making
loud, obnoxious noises.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.750
The pranks were so popular, similar behavior
was referred to as “doing a Dahmer.”

00:04:07.750 --> 00:04:10.750
By the end of his high school, Dahmer’s
parents’ troubled marriage finally came

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.710
to an end after an unsuccessful attempt at
counseling.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.380
In early 1978, Lionel moved out of the house.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.550
Dahmer graduated in May the same year.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:23.180
A few weeks after graduation, Dahmer committed
his first murder when he picked up a hitchhiker.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.170
Eighteen-year-old Steven Mark Hicks was on
his way to a rock concert when Dahmer lured

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.190
him back to his house to hang out and drink
a few beers before the show.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:34.760
By now, Dahmer lived alone at his parents’
house -- his mother had moved out with younger

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:38.340
brother David while his father took up residence
at a local motel.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.740
Hicks and Dahmer spent a few hours together
listening to music and drinking.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.640
When Hicks was ready to leave, Dahmer didn’t
want him too, so he struck him in the head

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.040
with a 10 lb.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.770
dumbbell and strangled him to death while
Hicks was unconscious.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:55.660
He then masturbated over his body, moved him
to the crawl space under the house and dissected

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:59.060
his body before burying it in a shallow grave.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:03.990
Several weeks later, Dahmer unearthed Hicks’
body, pared the flesh from the bones and dissolved

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:04.990
it in acid.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:09.330
He crushed Hicks’ bones with a sledgehammer
and scattered them all in the woodlot behind

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.330
the house.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.920
A short time later, Dahmer’s father visited
his son and learned he was living alone.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.870
He moved back in the house and convinced Dahmer
to enroll in college.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:21.570
Dahmer spent three months at Ohio State University
before dropping out.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:25.790
In early 1979, at the urging of his father,
he joined the U.S. Army.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.240
Dahmer served as a combat medic in Germany
but his performance deteriorated due to his

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.240
drinking.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:34.070
He was honorably discharged in March of 1981.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:39.740
At least two soldiers later attested Dahmer
raped them while in the service — one repeatedly

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.360
over the course of 17 months and the other
once after Dahmer drugged him.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:43.360
Killing Spree

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:50.380
“The only motive that there ever was was
to completely control a person; a person I

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.300
found physically attractive.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:06:04.460
And keep them with me as long as possible,
even if it meant just keeping a part of them.”

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:08.620
Following his discharge, Dahmer returned home
to Ohio but stayed only a brief time.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:12.690
He was arrested for disorderly conduct which
prompted his father to arrange for Dahmer

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.740
to live with his grandmother in Wisconsin.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.610
His alcoholism continued and he was arrested
for indecent exposure.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:23.470
He was arrested again in 1986 when two boys
accused him of masturbating in front of them.

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:28.960
In September of 1987, Dahmer took his second
victim, Steven Tuomi.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.960
According to Dahmer, he has no memory of killing
Tuomi -- they had checked into a hotel room

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.020
together and drank heavily...when Dahmer woke
in the morning he discovered Tuomi’s dead

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.050
body, with blood on his hands.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:42.490
Dahmer bought a large suitcase to transport
Tuomi's remains to his grandmother's basement,

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:46.700
where he dismembered and masturbated on the
corpse before disposing of the remains.

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:50.760
Only after Dahmer killed another two victims
at his grandmother’s home did she tire of

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:53.440
her grandson's late nights and drunkenness
— although she had no knowledge of his other

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.889
activities — and she forced him to move
out of the premises in 1988.

00:06:57.889 --> 00:07:03.169
That September 1989, Dahmer had an extremely
lucky escape: An encounter with a 13-year-old

00:07:03.169 --> 00:07:08.190
Laotian boy resulted in charges of sexual
exploitation and second-degree sexual assault

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.190
for Dahmer.

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:12.090
He pleaded guilty, claiming that the boy had
appeared much older.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:17.000
While awaiting sentencing for his sexual assault
case, Dahmer again put his grandmother's basement

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:23.290
to gruesome use: In March 1989, he lured,
drugged, strangled, sodomized, photographed,

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.770
dismembered and disposed of Anthony Sears,
an aspiring model.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:32.410
At his trial for child molestation in May
1989, Dahmer was the model of contrition,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:37.030
arguing eloquently, in his own defense, about
how he had seen the error of his ways, and

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:39.560
that his arrest marked a turning point in
his life.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.540
His defense counsel argued that he needed
treatment, not incarceration, and the judge

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:48.320
agreed, handing down a one-year prison sentence
on "day release" — allowing Dahmer to work

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:52.700
at his job during the day and return to the
prison at night — as well as a five-year

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.610
probationary sentence.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:58.960
Years later, in an interview with CNN, Lionel
Dahmer stated that he wrote a letter to the

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:04.060
court that issued the sentence, requesting
psychological help before his son's parole.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.310
However, Jeffrey Dahmer was granted an early
release by the judge, after serving only 10

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.409
months of his sentence.

00:08:09.409 --> 00:08:13.100
He briefly lived with his grandmother following
his release, during which time he does not

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:16.970
appear to have added to his body count, before
moving back into his own apartment.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:21.290
Over the following two years, Dahmer's victim
count accelerated, bringing his total from

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.169
four to 17.

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:28.040
He developed rituals as he progressed, experimenting
with chemical means of disposal and often

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:30.950
consuming the flesh of his victims.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:34.450
Dahmer also attempted crude lobotomies, drilling
into victims' skulls while they were still

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.589
alive and injecting them with muriatic acid.

00:08:37.589 --> 00:08:43.500
He was careful to select victims on the fringes
of society, who were often itinerant or borderline

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.339
criminal, making their disappearances less
noticeable and reducing the likelihood of

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:48.339
his capture.

00:08:48.339 --> 00:08:52.120
As the murders piled up, Dahmer was still
unsatisfied, he said later:

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.150
“I was completely swept along with my own
compulsion.

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:56.880
I don't know how else to put it.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:01.060
It didn't satisfy me completely, so maybe
I was thinking, 'Maybe another one will.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:02.190
Maybe this one will.'

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:07.420
And the numbers started growing and growing
and just got out of control, as you can see.”

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:12.070
On May 27, 1991, Dahmer's neighbor Sandra
Smith called the police to report that an

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.420
Asian boy was running naked in the street.

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:18.500
When the police arrived, the boy was incoherent,
and they accepted the word of Dahmer — a

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.350
white man in a largely poor African-American
community — that the boy was his 19-year-old

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:24.350
lover.

00:09:24.350 --> 00:09:30.400
In fact, the boy was 14 years old and a brother
of the Laotian teen Dahmer had molested three

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.400
years earlier.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:34.480
The police escorted Dahmer and the boy home
and, clearly not wishing to become embroiled

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:39.280
in a homosexual domestic disturbance, took
only a cursory look around before leaving.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:43.860
Once the police left the scene, Dahmer killed
the boy and proceeded with his usual rituals.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:48.890
Had they conducted even a basic search, police
officers would have found the body of Dahmer's

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:50.730
12th victim, Tony Hughes.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:10:00.110
Before he was finally arrested, on July 22,
1991, he killed four more men.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:06.820
The Crime Scene

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:10.980
Dahmer's killing spree ended when he was arrested
on July 22, 1991.

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:15.470
That day, two Milwaukee police officers picked
up Tracy Edwards, a 32-year-old African American

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:19.380
man who was wandering the streets with a handcuff
dangling from his wrist.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.660
They decided to investigate the man's claims
that a "weird dude" had drugged and restrained

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:24.660
him.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:27.620
They arrived at Dahmer's apartment, where
he calmly offered to get the keys for the

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:28.620
handcuffs.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.340
Edwards claimed that the knife Dahmer had
threatened him with was in the bedroom.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:36.100
When the officer went in to corroborate the
story, he noticed Polaroid photographs of

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:39.260
dismembered bodies lying around.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:41.080
Dahmer was subdued by the officers.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.280
Subsequent searches revealed a head in the
refrigerator, three more in the freezer and

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:50.800
a catalog of other horrors, including preserved
skulls, jars containing genitalia and an extensive

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:54.390
gallery of macabre Polaroid photographs of
his victims.

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:59.740
Dahmer’s refrigerator and Polaroid photographs
became inextricably associated with his notorious

00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:00.740
killing spree.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:05.430
In 1996, following Dahmer’s death, a group
of Milwaukee businessmen raised more than

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:11.650
$400,000 to purchase the items he used for
his victims — including blades, saws, handcuffs

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:14.050
and a refrigerator to store body parts.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:17.779
They promptly destroyed them in an effort
to distance the city from the horrors of Dahmer's

00:11:17.779 --> 00:11:21.279
actions and the ensuing media circus surrounding
his trial.

00:11:21.279 --> 00:11:31.730
Trial and Imprisonment

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:35.160
Jeffrey Dahmer’s trial began in January
1992.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:39.670
Given that the majority of Dahmer's victims
were African American, there were considerable

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:44.690
racial tensions and so strict security precautions
were taken, including an eight-foot barrier

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:47.560
of bulletproof glass that separated him from
the gallery.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:52.110
The inclusion of only one African American
on the jury provoked further unrest, but was

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:54.580
ultimately contained and short lived.

00:11:54.580 --> 00:11:58.480
Lionel Dahmer and his second wife attended
the trial throughout.

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:02.390
Dahmer initially pleaded not guilty to all
charges, despite having confessed to the killings

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:07.620
during police interrogation, but he eventually
changed his plea to guilty by virtue of insanity.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:13.089
His defense then offered the gruesome details
of his behavior, as proof that only someone

00:12:13.089 --> 00:12:16.089
insane could commit such terrible acts.

00:12:16.089 --> 00:12:19.860
Dahmer later said in an interview, “It's
hard for me to believe that a human being

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:23.770
could have done what I've done, but I know
that I did it.”

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:28.620
The jury chose to believe the prosecution's
assertion that Dahmer was fully aware that

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.410
his acts were evil and chose to commit them
anyway.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:36.630
On February 15, 1992, they returned after
approximately 10 hours' deliberation to find

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.390
him guilty, but sane, on all counts.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:44.850
He was sentenced to 15 consecutive life terms
in prison, with a 16th term tacked on in May.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:46.240
“It is now over.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.690
This has never been a case of trying to get
free.

00:12:48.690 --> 00:12:50.160
I didn't ever want freedom.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:51.160
Frankly, I wanted death for myself.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.240
This was a case to tell the world that I did
what I did, but not for reasons of hate.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.420
I hated no one.

00:12:56.420 --> 00:12:59.370
I knew I was sick or evil or both.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:01.050
Now I believe I was sick.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.430
The doctors have told me about my sickness,
and now I have some peace.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:06.370
I know how much harm I have caused...

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:09.430
Thank God there will be no more harm that
I can do.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.240
I believe that only the Lord Jesus Christ
can save me from my sins...

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:15.649
I ask for no consideration.”

00:13:15.649 --> 00:13:19.220
Dahmer reportedly adjusted well to prison
life, although he was initially kept apart

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.620
from the general population.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:24.880
He eventually convinced authorities to allow
him to integrate more fully with other inmates.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:28.920
He found religion in the form of books and
photos sent to him by his father, and he was

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:39.980
granted permission by the Columbia Correctional
Institution to be baptized by a local pastor.

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:44.380
Final Days

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:49.180
On November 28, 1994, in accordance with his
inclusion in regular work details, Dahmer

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:53.600
was assigned to work with two other convicted
murderers, Jesse Anderson and Christopher

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.600
Scarver.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.149
After they had been left alone to complete
their tasks, guards returned to find that

00:13:58.149 --> 00:14:02.380
Scarver had brutally beaten both men with
a metal bar from the prison weight room.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.990
Dahmer was pronounced dead after approximately
one hour.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:08.660
Anderson succumbed to his injuries days later.

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:12.339
In 2015, Christopher Scarver spoke to the
New York Post about his reasons for killing

00:14:12.339 --> 00:14:13.339
Dahmer.

00:14:13.339 --> 00:14:17.120
Scarver alleged that he was disturbed not
only by Dahmer's crimes, but by a habit Dahmer

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:22.660
had developed of fashioning severed limbs
from prison food to antagonize other inmates.

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:26.450
After being taunted by Dahmer and Anderson
during their work detail, Scarver said that

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:30.530
he confronted Dahmer about his crimes before
beating the two men to death.

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:33.580
He also claimed that prison guards allowed
the murders to happen by

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:37.830
In Dahmer's will, he had requested upon his
death that his body be cremated as soon as

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:41.769
possible, but some medical researchers wanted
his brain preserved so it could be studied.

00:14:41.769 --> 00:14:46.060
Lionel Dahmer wanted to respect his son's
wishes and cremate all remains of his son.

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:48.230
His mother felt his brain should go to research.

00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:51.440
The two parents went to court and a judge
sided with Lionel.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:54.020
After over a year Dahmer's body was released
from being held as evidence and the remains

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:56.210
were cremated as he had requested.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:15:01.360
In August 2012, nearly two decades after his
death, it was reported his childhood home

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:05.950
in Bath, Ohio — where he committed his first
murder in 1978, and buried his victim's remains

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.230
— was on the market.

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:11.800
Its owner, musician Chris Butler, stated that
the property would make a great home, as long

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.769
as the buyer could "get past the horror factor."

00:15:14.769 --> 00:15:20.330
In March 2016, Butler put the house up for
rent for $8,000 for the week of the Republican

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:21.770
National Convention.

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:42.230
As of July 2017, the house was no longer listed
on the market, according 

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:59.600
to Zillow.com.

